WEBVTT

00:00:11.014 --> 00:00:13.808
HERMIONE: Are you thinking
there's a Horcrux in Bellatrix's vault?

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.478
HARRY: She was terrified when she
thought we'd been in there.

00:00:16.519 --> 00:00:18.521
She kept asking you
what else we'd taken.

00:00:18.563 --> 00:00:21.608
I bet you there's a Horcrux in there,
another piece of his soul.

00:00:21.649 --> 00:00:24.736
Let's find it and kill it,
we're one step closer to killing him.

00:00:24.778 --> 00:00:26.696
RON:
And what happens when we find it?

00:00:26.738 --> 00:00:30.283
How are we supposed to destroy it
now you've given the sword to Griphook?

00:00:30.325 --> 00:00:32.368
HARRY:
I'm still working on that part.

00:00:34.704 --> 00:00:35.997
He's weak.

00:00:45.298 --> 00:00:47.008
Yes?

00:00:48.718 --> 00:00:52.972
Mr. Ollivander, I need to ask you
a few questions.

00:00:53.014 --> 00:00:55.809
OLLIVANDER:
Anything, my boy, anything.

00:00:56.768 --> 00:00:59.479
HARRY:
Would you mind identifying this wand?

00:00:59.521 --> 00:01:02.148
We need to know if it's safe to use.

00:01:08.071 --> 00:01:09.864
Walnut.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.326
Dragon heartstring.

00:01:13.952 --> 00:01:16.746
Twelve and three-quarter inches.

00:01:17.705 --> 00:01:19.541
Unyie--

00:01:21.626 --> 00:01:23.294
Unyielding.

00:01:24.379 --> 00:01:28.758
This belonged to Bellatrix Lestrange.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.594
Treat it carefully.

00:01:32.345 --> 00:01:33.596
And this?

00:01:36.975 --> 00:01:38.893
Hawthorn.

00:01:40.186 --> 00:01:42.939
And unicorn hair.

00:01:42.981 --> 00:01:47.652
Ten inches. Reasonably pliant.

00:01:51.197 --> 00:01:55.743
This was the wand of Draco Malfoy.

00:01:56.452 --> 00:01:59.080
Was? Is it not still?

00:01:59.122 --> 00:02:03.251
Well, perhaps not, if you won it from him.

00:02:05.628 --> 00:02:09.257
I sense its allegiance has changed.

00:02:13.928 --> 00:02:18.850
You talk about wands
as if they have feelings...

00:02:20.768 --> 00:02:22.061
...can think.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.903
The wand chooses the wizard, Mr. Potter.

00:02:30.445 --> 00:02:35.408
That much has always been clear
to those of us who have studied wandlore.

00:02:37.118 --> 00:02:39.954
And what do you know
about the Deathly Hallows?

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:48.129
It is rumored there are three:

00:02:49.881 --> 00:02:51.966
The Elder Wand...

00:02:52.717 --> 00:02:58.097
...the Cloak of Invisibility
to hide you from your enemies...

00:02:58.139 --> 00:03:04.103
...and the Resurrection Stone
to bring back loved ones from the dead.

00:03:04.145 --> 00:03:09.275
Together, they make one
the master of death.

00:03:09.317 --> 00:03:15.531
But few truly believe
that such objects exist.

00:03:15.573 --> 00:03:17.242
HARRY:
Do you?

00:03:17.825 --> 00:03:19.994
Do you believe they exist, sir?

00:03:23.331 --> 00:03:30.129
I see no reason to put stock
into an old wives' tale.

00:03:30.588 --> 00:03:31.798
You're lying.

00:03:33.049 --> 00:03:35.385
You know one exists.

00:03:35.426 --> 00:03:37.387
You told him about it.

00:03:37.428 --> 00:03:42.976
You told him about the Elder Wand
and where he could go looking for it.

00:03:46.437 --> 00:03:48.564
He tortured me.

00:03:51.192 --> 00:03:53.069
Besides...

00:03:54.028 --> 00:03:56.781
...I only conveyed rumors.

00:03:58.533 --> 00:04:00.076
There's....

00:04:01.286 --> 00:04:04.455
There's no telling whether he will find it.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.377
He has found it, sir.

00:04:15.258 --> 00:04:17.051
We'll let you rest.

00:04:19.595 --> 00:04:21.973
OLLIVANDER:
He's after you, Mr. Potter.

00:04:22.473 --> 00:04:28.396
If it's true, what you say,
and he has the Elder Wand...

00:04:30.231 --> 00:04:31.899
...I'm afraid...

00:04:32.483 --> 00:04:35.403
...you really don't stand a chance.

00:04:36.612 --> 00:04:40.199
Well, I suppose I'll have to kill him
before he finds me, then.

00:04:45.413 --> 00:04:47.623
RON:
Are you sure that's hers?

00:04:49.375 --> 00:04:50.918
Positive.

00:04:56.966 --> 00:04:58.593
Well?

00:04:59.635 --> 00:05:01.512
How do I look?

00:05:01.888 --> 00:05:03.598
RON:
Hideous.

00:05:04.265 --> 00:05:07.518
You can give that to Hermione to hold,
all right, Griphook?

00:05:27.372 --> 00:05:28.623
We're relying on you.

00:05:28.664 --> 00:05:32.752
If you get us past the guards
and into the vault, the sword's yours.

00:05:45.264 --> 00:05:46.557
Madam Lestrange.

00:05:46.599 --> 00:05:48.393
HERMIONE:
Good morning.

00:05:49.685 --> 00:05:53.439
GRIPHOOK:
"Good morning"? "Good morning"?

00:05:53.481 --> 00:05:56.692
You're Bellatrix Lestrange,
not some dewy-eyed school girl.

00:05:56.734 --> 00:05:58.569
RON:
Hey. Easy.

00:05:58.611 --> 00:06:03.324
She gives us away, we might as well
use that sword to slit our own throats.

00:06:03.366 --> 00:06:05.368
Understand?

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:08.871
No, he's right. I was being stupid.

00:06:09.122 --> 00:06:10.623
HARRY:
Okay.

00:06:10.873 --> 00:06:12.542
Let's do it.

